<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pedro Caetano Pereira</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">19th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pedro Caetano Pereira was a ruler of Makanga, an Afro-Portuguese warlord state north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tete">Tete</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a>. With his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goncalo-caetano-pereira">Gonçalo Caetano Pereira</a> he built the state in the mid-19th century as the Portuguese prazo system broke down, ruling from fortified stockades called aringas and relying on armed slave soldiers.</p></div>
